The prototype and study make three main contributions: 
• A cost-conscious PLC-based control architecture that implements discrete-time PID pH control and proportional alum dosing suitable for IEC 61131-3 PLCs, validated on a 200 L Universitas Brawijaya pilot rig under variable influent conditions; 
• A control and sensing calibration procedure that yields \balum dosing accuracy of 98.2%\b and a closed-loop pH regulation of \b7.20 \pm 0.05\b with a median settling time of \b12.3 s\b; 
• An experimental dataset from N = 50 reproducible trials (influent turbidity 10–60 NTU, influent pH 5.8–8.4) showing \baverage turbidity removal of 95.4%\b and a quantified failure mode analysis under edge disturbances (performance drop < 3%).
